<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: AIB's FMB Q4 earnings up 14 pct.</title>
<headline>AIB's FMB Q4 earnings up 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million $ unless stated)</p>
<p> Net income		    36.03		  vs 31.49</p>
<p> Net interest income	 105.25		 vs 99.84</p>
<p> Total interest income     185.37		 vs 186.55</p>
<p> Total interest expense    80.12		  vs 86.71</p>
<p> Total non-interest income 56.83		  vs 52.14</p>
<p> Total non-interest expense105.36		 vs 98.37</p>
<p> Income before income tax  56.22		  vs 47.94</p>
<p> Income tax expense	  20.14		  vs 16.45</p>
<p>Results for year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p> Net income		    132.34		 vs 120.19</p>
<p> Net interest income	 403.71		 vs 392.99</p>
<p> Total interest income     719.03		 vs 707.54</p>
<p> Total interest expense    315.32		 vs 314.55</p>
<p> Total non-interest income 216.89		 vs 195.91</p>
<p> Total non-interest expense406.86		 vs 388.72</p>
<p> Income before income tax  207.24		 vs 184.18</p>
<p> Income tax expense	  74.85		  vs 63.99</p>
<p>NOTE - First Maryland Bancorp is wholly-owned by Allied Irish Banks Plc. </p>
<p>AIB said underlying loan growth at December 1996 was 11 percent higher than the previous year when adjusted for the securitisation last April of an additional $335 million of credit card receivables and the impact of FMB's $83.5 million acquisition of First Washington Bancorp.</p>
<p>AIB said asset quality at FMB continued to be strong with non-performing assets reducing to $59.0 million, which amounts to 0.55 percent of total assets.</p>
<p>Non-performing loans of $45.8 million were covered 338 percent by total provisions of $154.8 million.</p>
<p>Earlier, AIB announced that FMB would acquire Dauphin Deposit Corp for $43 a share or $1.36 billion.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
